# Python and Markdown quality

These rules prevent compressed files and hidden character warnings.

## Python formatting

- Python files must be normal multiline source code
- Never write a whole Python module as one line
- import, class, function, and method blocks must use normal newlines
- Use clear indentation and readable spacing
- Keep line length reasonable, target less than 140 characters

## Markdown and MDC formatting

- Markdown and MDC files must be multiline text
- Never compress a document into one line
- Prefer plain ASCII punctuation in rules and docs

## Hidden and bidi Unicode

- Do not add hidden or bidirectional Unicode characters
- Avoid zero-width and direction override characters
- Use plain UTF-8 text with visible characters

## Validation after Python edits

- Run python -m pytest
- Resolve failures before commit and PR update
